omx-contract (3.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Schema 3.1.0: a words item may name the items its words take a unit and a
    basis from (units, bases) and declare an extension (the id of a CLAP
    extension and the prefix and namespace of LV2 properties); a word may carry
    a unit and a basis. The validator refuses a unit or basis that is no word
    of the item named (word-unit, word-basis).
  * The resource hints (docs/resource-hints.md): RESOURCE_HINTS declares the
    seven hints a plugin states about its own footprint, each with its
    resource, unit and basis, and the flag unit joins RESOURCE_UNITS. The CLAP
    draft org.openmixer.resource-hints.draft/0 is rendered as
    omxcontract/omx_resource_hints.h and the LV2 properties of the omxres
    namespace as share/omx-contract/omx-resource-hints.ttl, by the new
    render --target lv2. The ts and json renders carry the item. Each carrier
    has a conformance test with a sabotage.
  * Schema 3.1.0 also lets a words item name the item its words are drawn on
    (axes); a word then names its x and y, and an axis word states its unit
    and scale. The validator refuses a missing or unknown axis (word-axis)
    and an axis with no unit or scale (axis).
  * The curve kinds (docs/curves.md): CURVE_KINDS declares the eight kinds of
    picture a panel draws, each with its two axes, and CURVE_AXES each axis's
    unit and scale. The five graph kinds of the omx-plugins schema are kept;
    comb-response, modulation-shape (the picture lfo stood for) and
    interval-map are added for the remaining-FX wave (#107).
  * Per-band readouts (docs/readouts.md): band<n> and the one-band name,
    numbered from 1 in order with no gap and drawn alike; the validator
    refuses a gap, a band out of order or a band drawn unlike the others
    (readout-band). The grammar names the wave's readouts: band1GainDb to
    band6GainDb, band1GainReductionDb to band5GainReductionDb, attackGainDb
    and sustainGainDb, declared by omx-dsp's kernel files.
  * The unit dB/oct, a slope in dB per octave, for the key tilt of the
    compressor and the gate (FreeMixer/omx-dsp#188); cents, which the
    doubler's detune needs, was already a unit.
  * It breaks nothing new: libomxdsp-dev before 0.25.0, libomx-clap-core-dev
    before 0.13.0 and omx-plugins-dev before 0.13.0 stay the floors.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0200

omx-contract (3.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Schema major 3: the word formerly (a list's former name) and the word
    c.alias (a travel's second C spelling) are removed, x-omx-schema-version
    is 3.0.0, an installed file's $schema is the v3 URL and the reader reads
    contract.d/3/ only.
  * The hosting codes leave: the 16 data/hosting files move to omx-clap-core
    byte for byte, installed as contract.d/3/omx-clap-core/hosting/.
    omx_vocabulary.h, the JSON render, the vocabulary schema and the ts golden
    hold no hosting code; omx-clap-core renders them with render --package
    omx-clap-core, under the C names omx_vocabulary.h gave them.
  * render --target c|ts --package <pkg> also writes the package's vocabulary
    (<stem>_vocabulary.h, <stem>-vocabulary.js and .d.ts): every codes and
    words item of its files with no render word, spelled as the whole read
    spells it, a code by its code, never by its key.
  * The default EQ rule leaves for omx-dsp (#1841): lib/eq-defaults.mjs, the
    C render's omx_eq_default_centres() and omx_eq_default_type(), the ts
    module's eqDefault exports and the validator's three EQ rules. The file
    word checks declares a budget (a sum of named numbers held at or under a
    named one), and a count sheet's default is held inside its min and max.
  * Descriptor words: extensions (a per-format bag, carried verbatim),
    plugin.doc, the ratio unit, and the item kind formatMap (a format's
    source fields, each mapped to a word, carried as an extension or dropped
    by a named ruling).
  * It breaks libomxdsp-dev before 0.25.0, libomx-clap-core-dev before 0.13.0
    and omx-plugins-dev before 0.13.0, the releases built against schema 3.

